x86_64-linux  A closure type has no name the standard obliges anybody to match - [expr.prim.lambda] - and cxx1 numbers its closures `$_N` in the order written where clang writes `UliiE_` on Itanium and `<lambda_N>` for the Microsoft ABI, the shape lambda.nonames records; nothing links against a closure's call operator. Every other name agrees. And clang emits only the C2 of a constructor defined inside its class here, where cxx1 emits C1 beside it: Sorter's and Derived's.
